From: Lotfix
Subject: [PATCH] output: follow Anland output resizes (tablet rotation)

Anland resizes its output when the Android device rotates. Hyprland only
honours a sized state event for user-created outputs; accept it when ANLAND
is set, so the monitor follows portrait and landscape.
---
diff --git a/src/output/Monitor.cpp b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
index e69d8dd..1b63af8 100644
--- a/src/output/Monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
@@ -225,7 +225,8 @@ void CMonitor::onConnect(bool noRule) {
             return;
         }
 
-        if (!m_createdByUser)
+        // Anland: Android resizes the output when the tablet rotates; follow it like a user-created output.
+        if (!m_createdByUser && !getenv("ANLAND"))
             return;
 
         const auto SIZE = event.size;
